DTSTAMP:20261010T053424Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T150000
SUMMARY:Creating Custom Code Execution Engine Sandboxes For Your Loops And
  Harnesses
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nThe last session showed how agent s
 warms can run safely on disposable\, hardware-isolated compute.\n\nThis se
 cond session covers building the custom sandboxes that those agents need.\
 n\nSee how to package your own runtimes\, dependencies\, and tools as a cu
 stom container\, expose it through Azure Container Apps Sandboxes\, and op
 erate it as a fast\, isolated execution service.\n\nWatch a custom engine 
 move from container image to a managed session pool that agents can invoke
  on demand.\n\nYou'll learn • When to choose a custom sandbox\n• How t
 o package specialized runtimes\, libraries\, binaries\, and tools\n• Con
 figuring prewarmed capacity\, lifecycle policies\, health probes\, and aut
 omatic cleanup\n• Securing execution with isolation\, network controls\,
  managed identity\, and tenant-aware session identifiers\n• Monitoring e
 ngine health\, capacity\, lifecycle events\, and application output with A
 zure Monitor\n\n[Explore the Build Cloud Native Apps series](https://devel
 oper.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1692?wt.mc_id=meetup_27397_webpage_rea
 ctor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3160
 09181/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T201653Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260806T201653Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
